===Golden Skin Strategies===
*'''For the first quest''', try going towards Floor 20+, since Twisted Bassie is guaranteed to spawn every [[Floor]] that is a multiple of 20, not to mention Twisted Bassie being able to spawn before Floor 20 too. You can play with a distractor such as {{CI|Looey|name=true}} or {{CI|Eclipse|name=true}} to make the progression easier and to let them bring Twisted Bassie to the elevator for the encounter, though despite the difficulty you can still do this solo.
*'''For the second quest''', you should find a team with good players and play, or you can have a few friends carry you. If you plan on helping with extracting, or if you plan on going solo, equip Trinkets like {{TI|Mime Makeup|name=true}} to minimize the risk of any loose Twisteds coming after you.
*'''For the third quest''', you can just join a run, but refrain from voting the {{CDI|Air Freshener|name=true}} Card, instead go for {{CDI|Piping Tape|name=true}} and the {{CDI|Electrician|name=true}} Cards, as they would heighten the chance for [[Spring Fever]] Floors.

==Strategies==
At first glance, Bassie seems to fit into the role of a distractor, having maximum [[Movement Speed]] and very high [[Stamina]]. However, because of her unique [[Abilities]] and 4{{Star}} [[Stealth]], she is best played as a survivalist/support [[Toon]] rather than a pure distractor. With that said, she may fit into the role of a backup distractor depending on your team's average Stealth and how experienced they are. She makes an extremely good survivalist due to her superior mobility stats, Stealth, and additional [[Item]] slot.

Due to Bassie's abysmal Extraction Speed and Skill Check stats, it is recommended to mostly avoid [[Machines]] and instead use her excellent survivability for your team's benefit. However, if there are any [[Treadmill Machines]], Bassie is one of the best extractors for them, due to her extremely potent mobility Stats. She can also help with Duo Machines, though preferably only if you are good at hitting her tiny [[Skill Checks]], as her below average [[Extraction Speed]] would be combined with another [[Toon]]'s Extraction Speed, together totaling to a great minimum about the equivalent of 5 Stars or more.

Because of her Abilities that grant four inventory slots and enable her to drop Items without penalty, Bassie is an amazing team supporter and offers new ways for Toons to approach Floors. This is primarily done by storing Items for future Floors, or helping out fellow Toons by gifting them important Items such as {{II|Box o' Chocolates|name=false|plural=a}}, {{II|Health Kit|name=false}}s, or {{II|Smoke Bomb|name=false}}s.

It's beneficial to give [[Toons]] Items that aid with their weaknesses, such as giving {{CI|Rodger|name=true}} a {{II|Speed Candy|name=false}}, or collecting 'worthless' Items for a {{CI|Sprout|name=true}}/{{CI|Ginger|name=true}} to get more {{Tape|name=true}}. Furthermore, a strategy is to gather all Items on the Floor and leave them at certain locations, such as leaving {{II|Skill Check Candy|name=false|plural=a}} and {{II|Extraction Speed Candy|name=false|plural=a}} next to incomplete Machines, and leaving all other Items nearby the Elevator for others to grab during [[Panic Mode]]. Additionally, if {{CI|Twisted Gigi|name=true}} is on the [[Floor]], you can either drop your valuable Items in a safe spot or simply in front of the [[Elevator]] to avoid them being taken, though you either need Twisted Gigi occupied or your Items guarded due to her ability to take Items off the floor, rearrange them to let least valuable Items go first, or embrace it and act as delivery for any lost Items, maybe even transport Items between Toons more conveniently.

Stamina, Speed, and survival Items should be dropped in the loops/in front of struggling Toons/distractors, especially if they use an Item, freeing up space. They should also be provided to low-mobility Toons after they escape, as they may need more immediately afterwards. Leave any extras near the Elevator so Toons can reach them in time. You can also put these near Treadmill Machines so Toons can finish them faster.

As for heals, Bassie should be used to deliver {{II|Bandage|name=false}}s and Health Kits to distractors so they don't have to leave their loops. She acts as storage for these, similarly to Cosmo, even if she can't "split" Health Kits. She should always buy heals when able. Generally, Bassie should prioritize Bandages and Cosmo should prioritize Health Kits if either of the Toons are present, but making them split these Items makes access to healing Items more efficient for your teammates, so try not to let one of them hog all of the healing Items. When in doubt, Bassie can always drop them for Cosmo later, can pick them up faster, and can hold onto more Items safely, so she can function as their second inventory.

Extraction Items can be delivered to Toons you notice working on Machines (especially if they free up space) or held onto if you intend to work on Machines yourself. {{II|Jumper Cable|name=false}}s and {{II|Valve|name=false}}s can be used yourself, as they offer the same value no matter who uses them. In fact, you can sprint to a Machine near a distractor and use them there so Toons don't need to go there/stay there for less time.

Due to her Ability synergizing with Trinkets related to picking up Items, Bassie has the potential to become very mobile, as she can constantly drop and pick up Items in order to activate either {{TI|Bone|name=true}}'s 25% Movement Speed bonus or {{TI|Feather Duster|name=true}}'s 20 Stamina unit regeneration. Bone's increase has the potential to make her one of the fastest Toons in the game, outpacing even the likes of {{CI|Looey|name=true}} at 1{{Heart}} or {{CI|Eclipse|name=true}} in a [[Blackout]] with really good timing, as picking up too often (yet also not often enough) can drop your speed boost down to 6.7%. Feather Duster can basically give Bassie infinite Stamina, but this is of course once again dependent on timing. Overall, doing this can require a lot of focus, so try to practice before using these techniques in a proper run.

Bassie is incredible at support and survival, with a strong emphasis on team gameplay. She is a great choice if you can stay on top of supporting and communicating with teammates. Being able to adapt practically any Item into being useful by giving it to the right Toon.

===Trinket Combinations===
{{Preference}}
Recommended Trinket combinations for Bassie:

====Mobility====
*'''{{TI|Bone|name=true}} and {{TI|Feather Duster|name=true}}/Any'''
**With these Trinkets, by dropping and picking up [[Items]] quickly, Bassie gains extraordinary amounts of speed. This combination is often used to distract as Bassie, though it's only recommended in specific teams that have [[Toons]] with higher [[Stealth]].
*'''{{TI|Dog Plush|name=true}}/Options'''
**This Trinket alone allows Bassie to outwalk anything besides {{CI|Twisted Pebble|name=true}}, {{CI|Twisted Glisten|name=true}} when enraged, {{CI|Twisted Coal|name=true}} when a [[Blackout]] is present, and some others {{Small|(22 walk speed)}}. It's also an alternative to Bone and Feather Duster if one does not have the ability to constantly pick up Items to gain speed easily. Here are some options to pair Dog Plush with:
***'''{{TI|Speedy Shoes|name=true}}''', to further improve walk speed, more preferable for those new to distracting as Bassie {{Small|(23.1 walk speed)}};
***'''{{TI|Feather Duster|name=true}}''', to further improve stamina management if you do not have Bone, more preferable when against fast [[Twisteds]] like {{CI|Twisted Pebble|name=true}} for those new to distracting as Bassie;
***'''{{TI|Clown Horn|name=true}}/{{TI|Ribbon Spool|name=true}}''', to also out-walk before Panic Mode Twisted Glisten, Twisted Pebble, and Twisted Vee when you are inflicted with the {{Debuff|Slow|II}} [[Debuff]] when active {{Small|(24.2 walk/33 run speed)}}. Also good if you plan on duo-distracting;
***'''{{TI|Train Whistle|name=true}}''', to completely nullify the {{Debuff|Slow|}} Debuff, making {{CI|Twisted Vee|name=true}} significantly easier to distract;
***'''{{TI|Vanity Mirror|name=true}}''', to more easily and safely gather any secret stashed items during Panic Mode {{Small|(39 run speed)}};
****This is only recommended if you have unorganized teammates and must stash your items far away from the Elevator;
***'''{{TI|Scrapbook|name=true}}''', to avoid other 4{{Star}} [[Stealth]] Toons taking away the Twisteds' aggro;
****Do note that this Trinket will not lower your Stealth enough to be able to distract around 3 Star Stealth and below [[Toons]].
***Any of the Trinkets in the '''Extraction Section''', to help with [[Floor]] progression; etc.

====Extraction====
*The following Trinkets help Bassie deal with her main deficiency, that being her 1{{Star}} [[Skill Check]] and 2 Star [[Extraction Speed]]:
**'''{{TI|Vee's Remote|name=true}}''', to instantly complete Machines in dangerous locations, such as dead ends and open areas;
**'''{{TI|Mime Makeup|name=true}}''', to more safely extract by removing the danger of missing Skill Checks;
**'''{{TI|Thinking Cap|name=true}}''', to increase Skill Check Size, helping to fail less Skill Checks, though Mime Makeup can be more beneficial in some cases;
*If the player has no issues with small Skill Checks, they may consider using '''{{TI|Magnifying Glass|name=true}}''' or '''{{TI|Participation Award|name=true}}''' to help with [[Machine]] extraction more easily, even if the Skill Check window is far smaller. Though, do note that if the player has lag/missing frames, they may want to consider other Trinkets for team progression, as Bassie is typically better with Treadmill Machines.
**Any Trinkets listed in the '''Mobility''' section, to help with survival.

====Support====
*'''{{TI|Dandy Plush|name=true}}''', to allow Bassie to stock up on important Items earlier and continuously for half the cost so they can be shared with her teammates;
*'''{{TI|Memory Locket|name=true}}''', to help Bassie find and store healing Items for her team.
