==Trivia==
*Bassie is the third {{Type|Main}} to have the requirement of reaching [[Floor]] 20 for her [[Mastery]], the previous two being {{CI|Pebble|name=true}} and {{CI|Bobette|name=true}}.
*Upon release, Bassie's Active [[Ability]] was labeled as a ''Passive Ability''. This was later changed because a [[Main Character]] [[Toon]] should only have one Passive Ability.
**This made Bassie the first Main Character (and Toon in general) to have 2 Passive Abilities.
*Bassie is the only [[Event]] {{Type|Main}} [[Toon]] who never had 5{{Star}} in more than one [[Stat]] upon being added in game. {{CI|Gourdy|name=true}} has permanent 5 Stars in two Stats and [[Bobette]] formerly had 5 Stars in two Stats before having 1 Star from her [[Skill Check]] moved to [[Movement Speed]].
*Bassie's name could possibly be a portmanteau of the word "Basket" and the name "Cassie" or "Bessie".
*According to her dialogue with {{CI|Glisten|name=true}}, Bassie's favorite flowers are tulips, hyacinths, and lily flowers.
**Coincidentally, they are all toxic to bunnies, which could reflect Bassie's negative relationship with {{CI|Cocoa|name=true}}, though this may be unintentional.
**Additionally, yellow hyacinths are known to represent jealousy, envy, and contempt which may represent Bassie's complicated feelings.
*Bassie's friends appear to be {{CI|Flyte|name=true}}, {{CI|Shelly|name=true}}, {{CI|Eggson|name=true}}, and possibly [[Glisten]], based on her interactions or Gossips.
**Her relationship with [[Cocoa]] is one-sided, Bassie herself has a very conflicted perspective, seemingly not viewing her as a friend and instead a rival.
**Additionally, there is a common misconception that Bassie "hates" Cocoa, this concept being false. This is enforced by Bassie treating Cocoa kindly with actions such as hugs in the "[[Wilting]]" music video, and not showing any major signs of aggression until the final conclusion. Bassie simply feels an intense jealousy towards Cocoa that drives her to act beyond what she can control.
*Bassie is the first [[Toon]] to have an Active [[Ability]] with no cooldown.
**By spamming the Active Ability button, you would already have completed one of her 6 [[Mastery]] quests, along with granting an immediate 5 {{TI|Ichor|name=true}} upon use every floor.
**She is also the first [[Toon]] who doesn't speak when using their Active Ability.
*Bassie's [[Ability]] does not work with {{TI|Peppermint Icing|name=true}} likely because her Ability does not have a cooldown.
*Bassie is the second [[Holiday Toon]] to cost {{TI|Ichor|name=true}}, the first being [[Bobette]], and the third being [[Gourdy]].
**This is likely because the three are [[Event]] [[Main]] [[Toons]], and their requirements are the same: 3000 of their respective Event's [[Currency]], 2500 [[Ichor]], and 100% [[Research]] on their [[Twisted]] counterparts.
*Bassie is the third [[Toon]] to have 1 Star Skill Check, the first being {{CI|Shrimpo|name=true}}, the second being {{CI|Cosmo|name=true}}, and the fourth being {{CI|Blot|name=true}}.
*Bassie may be afraid of being replaced by [[Cocoa]] being the {{HT|Easter}} {{Type|Main}}, foreshadowed by one of her interactions with [[Bobette]], and the [[Notes#Delilah Keen|note]] from [[Delilah]] found on the [[Easter Floor]].
**The reason for this is likely because Cocoa is a lot more social, confident and outgoing, making her more appealing to the kids at [[Gardenview]].
**This is very likely referenced with the release of her official plush, being released alongside a Cocoa plush. Additionally, in a promo image for the plushies on the merch site, the Cocoa plush is front and center, while the Bassie plush is off to the side.
**Coincidentally, Bassie shares many similarities with Cocoa. They both have 4 Star Stealth and 2 Star Extraction Speed, along with [[Abilities]] involving dropping [[Items]]. They are both brown and 2 eyelashes on the underside of their eyes. They have similarly shaped mouths, though with Cocoa's appearing more like a squiggly smile, while Bassie's looks more cat or even rabbit-like. Bassie's handles could also somewhat resemble bunny ears. This however may be unintentional.
***It is also unknown if Bassie can lift her handles up to that extent on her own.
*Upon release, Bassie's [[Statistics|Skill Check]] size looked roughly 4 Stars, due to her having 135 Skill Check size for no reason. This was later fixed.
*Currently, Bassie, [[Pebble]], and {{CI|Waxwell|name=true}} are the only [[Toons]] to have 5 Star [[Movement Speed]], if not counting {{CI|Razzle & Dazzle|name=true}} on odd floors.
**The former two, alongside the other Holiday [[Main Characters]], are the only Main Characters to not have a [[Toon Handler]].
**Bassie is the only Toon with this Stat Star value to:
***Be an [[Event Toon]].
***Be female.
***Have above average [[Stealth]].
***Have below average [[Skill Check]].
***Not have an [[Ability]] with a 60 second cooldown.
*According to her interaction with {{CI|Gigi|name=true}}, Bassie collects pressed flowers. Pressing flowers is a hobby of hers, based on her interaction and [[Gossip]] about [[Flyte]] and the fact she carries pressed flowers in her head.
*In [[Bassie's Shop]], if the player has purchased a Toon License for every [[Easter Toon]] but her, her smile turns into a sad frown. But if you buy her after that, she gets confused, then happy again.
*Bassie's plushie looks slightly different compared to her main model. The green socks she wears is missing on her plushie's model.
*Despite {{TI|Fishing Rod|name=true}} before [[Changelog|v0.22.1]] saying it gave 3 random [[Items]], it gave Bassie 4 Items due to her Passive [[Ability]].
*According to her dialogue with {{CI|Brightney|name=true}}, Bassie may be afraid of the dark.
*Bassie has 2 different idle animations, one where she touches her basket handle, and another where she brushes off her skirt, similar to [[Bobette]].
**This makes her the third [[Toon]] to have 2 idles. The first being [[Glisten]], the second being {{CI|Yatta|name=true}}, and the fourth being [[Blot]].
*Currently, Bassie and [[Blot]] are the second slowest extractors in the game, with [[Shrimpo]] being the slowest.
*Bassie's last name is Bloomington, confirmed by [[Qwel]] in a stream on June 14, 2025.
**She was the first [[Event Main Character]] to have their last name revealed.
*Bassie is the sixth [[Toon]] to have them and their {{CI|Twisted Bassie}}[[Twisted Bassie|Twisted counterpart]] be in 2 separate thumbnails that were at one point used, with {{CI|Razzle & Dazzle|name=true}} & {{CI|Blot|name=true}} being first, {{CI|Sprout|name=true}} & [[Pebble]] being second, [[Shelly]] being third, {{CI|Gourdy|name=true}} being fourth, {{CI|Coal|name=true}} being fifth, {{CI|Goob|name=true}} being seventh, {{CI|Squirm|name=true}} being eighth, {{CI|Brusha|name=true}} being ninth if counting her {{Skin|Messy Canvas}} [[Skin]], {{CI|Ribecca|name=true}} being tenth if counting her {{Skin|QoM|toon=Ribecca}} [[Skin]], and eleventh being {{CI|Dandy|name=true}}.
**If counting unused thumbnails, [[Brightney]] would be the actual sixth.
*For some reason, the walking animations for {{Skin|Sunflower Patch}}, {{Skin|Egg Hunting}}, and {{Skin|Spring-Time}} are slower than Bassie's other [[Skins]]. Her arms also swing in a more lively way in her running animation. This might be a bug in-game.
**This appears to be a trend with [[Event]] [[Main Characters]] or just general reruns, as [[Bobette]]'s Skins added in the [[2025 Christmas Event]] (with the exception of her {{Skin|Hot Chocolate}} Skin) alter her animations somewhat.
*Bassie is the only [[Event]] [[Main]] [[Toon]] with a public full Icon.
*Bassie, like [[Gourdy]] and [[Bobette]], has her own holiday-related song, that being [[Wilting]].
**This song also reveals that Bassie has an official voice actor, which is OR30.
***This makes her the second [[Toon]], alongside [[Cocoa]], to have an official voice actor, the first three being the [[Christmas Toons]] (excluding [[Coal]]).
*Bassie is the fourth [[Toon]] who uses their head to store or contain something, being pressed flowers she collects.
*Currently, Bassie and [[Gourdy]] are the only two {{Type|Main}} [[Toons]] that don't have an interaction with each other. It is unknown if they will have interaction dialogues.
**This may also be because she is possibly scared of Gourdy, due to being a child and a Main Character, with her possibly having a negative mindset about herself being worse than a child.
***This also applies to [[Coal]] and {{CI|Cocoa|name=true}} (with {{CI|Eclipse|name=true}}), [[Flyte]] and {{CI|Ginger|name=true}} (with {{CI|Soulvester|name=true}}), with them possibly being afraid to interact with them due to being Halloween Toons.
*Bassie may have a negative opinion of [[Dandy]] based on her [[Gossip]] about him, where she openly makes a rude comment in reference to him.
**She could share this trait with {{CI|Vee|name=true}}, though not to the same extent, as well as a lack of known mutual dislike.
**However, this could've just been due to a lack of social awareness and bluntness, with her intention not being to insult him.
*Bassie still keeps her fourth inventory slot when she gets a non-[[Dandy]] mask in the [[Haunted Gala]], likely due to the complications of having that extra slot disappear.
*Bassie, alongside [[Bobette]], are the first Holiday Toons to have a dialogue with the Halloween Toons whose rarities are dissimilar from each other.

